{"assets":["/statement-assets/556e1808241c412821360a8fc541b6c7e182ded0f99b5899652ad4967c734768.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1065","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Make It Equal"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There is a toy building consisting of $$$n$$$ towers. Each tower consists of several cubes standing on each other. The $$$i$$$-th tower consists of $$$h_i$$$ cubes, so it has height $$$h_i$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's define operation "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"slice"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" on some height $$$H$$$ as following: for each tower $$$i$$$, if its height is greater than $$$H$$$, then remove some top cubes to make tower's height equal to $$$H$$$. Cost of one \"slice\" equals to the total number of removed cubes from all towers."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's name slice as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" one if its cost is lower or equal to $$$k$$$ ($$$k \\ge n$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/556e1808241c412821360a8fc541b6c7e182ded0f99b5899652ad4967c734768.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Calculate the minimum number of good slices you have to do to make all towers have the same height. Of course, it is always possible to make it so."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains two integers $$$n$$$ and $$$k$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$, $$$n \\le k \\le 10^9$$$) — the number of towers and the restriction on slices, respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ space separated integers $$$h_1, h_2, \\dots, h_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le h_i \\le 2 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the initial heights of towers."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one integer — the minimum number of good slices you have to do to make all towers have the same heigth."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 5\n3 1 2 2 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 5\n2 3 4 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example it's optimal to make $$$2$$$ slices. The first slice is on height $$$2$$$ (its cost is $$$3$$$), and the second one is on height $$$1$$$ (its cost is $$$4$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"1065C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1065/problem/C"}